    "body": "Escalating from effort:high to effort:max under work-issue step 4.\n\nThe full issue needs new collision geometry, not only dialog wiring. crates/sim/src/chuck.rs defines JawChuck with one grip_diameter shared by all jaws. JawChuck::solid builds equal outside-grip boxes. JawChuck::check checks adjacent jaws using that shared radius. ID grip, stepped jaws and independent jaw offsets need new shell construction and overlap validation that preserve the conservative steel envelope. The current fit_on_stock in crates/app/src/commands/accessory.rs uses a world-axis stock AABB and IDENTITY_Q; rotary-axis fitting needs a different frame calculation. These are new geometry algorithms, which the effort table places at max.\n\nNo production changes, commits, push or PR. The claim is released for an effort:max worker. Open PRs #1817 and #1738 touch the MCP skill reference in different rows from the chuck entry. The candidate UI pin is saved outside the repository at /tmp/1468-ui-pin.patch.\n\nReproduction: egui_app::fixture_accessory_tests::chuck_dialog_offers_fit_to_the_stock failed on unchanged production code with assertion: a chuck offers stock fitting. Result: 0 passed, 1 failed, 820 filtered out. The gate output is /tmp/1468-pin-red.txt and the full test failure is /tmp/1468-pin-ui-lib-red.txt on this worker. No mutation check or quick gate was run because implementation stopped at escalation.\n",
